"Create a file named semantics.txt. Formalize the semantics of the absolute value function using a small step operational semantics or a set of inference rules. Define the evaluation relation for integer expressions and the abs operation.One section of the example came out muddled — fixing it:Created `semantics.txt` with a small-step operational semantics:\n\n- **Syntax** — expressions `n`, `abs(e)`, `e1 + e2`; values are integer literals\n- **Evaluation relation** — `->` defined as the smallest relation closed under 6 inference rules: 3 congruence rules (S-ABS, S-ADD-L, S-ADD-R) and 3 reduction rules (R-ADD, R-ABS-POS, R-ABS-NEG)\n- **Key rules** — `abs(n) -> n` if `n >= 0` (R-ABS-POS); `abs(n) -> -n` if `n < 0` (R-ABS-NEG), with exclusive side conditions\n- **Derived properties** — progress, determinism, termination\n- **Correspondence** — explicitly maps each reduction rule back to the properties P1–P3 in `spec.txt`, plus a worked example derivation `abs(-3 + 1) -> abs(-2) -> 2`"